<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hung-e Azhdar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hong-e Azhdar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hung-e Azhdar is a rock relief near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izeh">Izeh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, carved in the Parthian period. It shows a horseman, usually taken to be a Parthian king, together with standing figures including a local ruler of Elymais, and is among the main monuments of the Elymaean kingdom.</p></div>
